<p>As I said in chat, I like how you came to frame the final element; it solved my issues about the PL researchers having access to the SCP file itself.</p>
<p>Content-wise though, I'm not feeling that portion. I would prefer something of substance in the file, with the note sprinkled in it, rather than the entire 'file' being said note.</p>
<p>It's also a little weak, because there's a bit of a tonal shift between it and the 'p.s.'; it begins with an <em>almost</em> spoopy level of threatening, and the 'p.s.' comes off as lighthearted and almost comedic.</p>
<p>Finally, as it was a late addition, O think it could use just a touch more foreshadowing in the interview. Novote for the time being.</p>
